{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The detour was rider-requested. Chat message MSG-02812-001 is sent by the RIDER at 10:19:39 and reads 'can we stop at Paya Lebar Square first, need to grab something' — an instruction that comes from the rider and names a specific, actionable place, satisfying POL-RD-04(a) and (c). The rider's own claim accepts the stop was asked for ('I only asked for a quick stop').",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[0].text",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The instruction is timely under POL-RD-04(b). The meter started at 10:18:39 and the message is timestamped 10:19:39, sixty seconds later — either before the vehicle left the optimal corridor or, at worst, within the three-minute window that limb allows.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02812", "EV-TRIP-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[0].sent_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The gps_trace corroborates the instruction, so the corroboration test in POL-RD-04 is met: the waypoint_hint resolved from the message (1.381532, 103.831811) is passed at a nearest-fix distance of 35.99 m, far inside the 200 m threshold, at fix index 54. Because the trace does corroborate the instruction, this is not the uncorroborated-instruction case in POL-RD-14 and no contradiction under POL-RD-10(7) arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02812", "EV-CHAT-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The distance POL-RD-04 excludes is the out-of-corridor run to the requested stop and back. The trace measures 13.52 km against a booked optimal of 10.4 km — an excess of 3.12 km (30.0%) — and the only off-corridor excursion on the record is the single requested waypoint, passed once, at fix 54. There is no off-route ERP gantry, no second waypoint hinted in the chat, and no pickup or dropoff amendment on the trip record to suggest any other detour, so the whole measured excess is attributable to the rider's instruction.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02812", "EV-TRIP-02812", "EV-CHAT-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With the rider-attributable excess excluded before the threshold is applied, no deviation survives POL-RD-01, and POL-RD-02 — which runs only where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01 and no exculpatory clause fully excuses it — is never reached. The outcome is NO_ACTION, which under POL-GEN-03 is party-relative: on this rider-filed dispute it leaves fare_breakdown.payment_status of CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd of 0.00 exactly as they stand, so nothing is refunded to the rider and nothing is taken back from the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02812", "EV-GPS-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has discharged the burden POL-RD-08 places on him once the rider shows an excess: he points to a specific artifact (EV-CHAT-02812) and a specific clause (POL-RD-04) that exonerates the detour, rather than a general assertion that the traffic was bad. The uncited-assertion rule in POL-RD-08 is therefore not engaged against him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pass-through correction is owed to the rider. The fare breakdown carries no ERP or toll lines at all (on-route, off-route and total all 0.00) and no airport surcharge, and POL-RD-09(3) provides independently that where the detour was rider-caused under POL-RD-04 no ERP refund is due.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no repeat-deviation pattern that could uplift the remedy against the driver. The measured excess is 30.0% of optimal and 3.12 km, so on no view is the deviation MATERIAL under POL-RD-01 (neither above 50% nor above 8.0 km), and POL-RD-06 is not triggered at all; in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 368, a ratio of 0 against the 0.05 gate, and POL-GEN-01 confines this test to exactly those two fields.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02812", "EV-GPS-02812"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you: this is a route-deviation dispute on trip TRP-02812 (RydeX, metered). The telemetry is clean — 107 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, 10-second sampling, so no POL-RD-07(a)–(c) impairment — and it measures 13.52 km against a booked optimal route of 10.4 km. That is an excess of 3.12 km, or 30.0% of optimal, so both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (above 20% and above 0.8 km) and a deviation is established on this trip's trace alone. The rider's claim that the trace establishes a deviation is accepted, and the trace figure, not the rounded trip-record copy of 13.5 km, governs.\n\nThe driver nonetheless has a complete answer under POL-RD-04. Chat message MSG-02812-001, sent by the rider at 10:19:39 — about a minute after the meter started at 10:18:39 and well before the waypoint was reached at 10:27:39 — reads 'can we stop at Paya Lebar Square first, need to grab something'. It comes from the rider, it is timely, and it names a specific, actionable place. The GPS trace corroborates it: the waypoint resolved from chat_message.waypoint_hint (1.381532, 103.831811) is passed within 35.99 m at fix 54, far inside the 200 m test, so this is not the uncorroborated-instruction case in POL-RD-14 and no POL-RD-10(7) contradiction arises. POL-RD-04 therefore applies, and it excludes the excess distance between the vehicle leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor.\n\nOn this record that excursion is the whole of the excess. The only off-corridor movement is the single requested waypoint, passed once, with no second waypoint hinted in the chat, no pickup or dropoff amendment on the trip record, and no ERP line in the fare breakdown at all (on-route, off-route and total all 0.00), so there is no other detour the excess could consist of. The requested point sits well off the booked corridor, and the added distance is the natural cost of going there and back. Excluding it leaves no excess meeting POL-RD-01, no deviation survives, and POL-RD-02 — which runs only where a deviation is established — is never reached.\n\nI reject the rider's argument that the driver failed to prove the size of the exonerated stretch. POL-RD-04 requires a corroborated rider instruction, not a separate detour-distance artifact; once the instruction is corroborated, the excursion is excluded by operation of the clause, and the driver discharged his POL-RD-08 burden by pointing to a specific artifact (EV-CHAT-02812) and a specific clause (POL-RD-04). The rider's complaint that they asked only for a 'quick stop, not a tour' does not change where the stop was: the place they named is off the booked route.\n\nThe rest of the record changes nothing. EV-ADVIS-02812-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and can carry no fact; POL-RD-13 is not engaged because the driver relies on no external traffic cause, so nothing turns on the absence of an advisory. No POL-RD-06 conduct referral arises: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 368 completed trips in 90 days, so no pattern is established, and the deviation is not MATERIAL in any event. POL-RD-09 corrects nothing — there are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines, and limb (3) bars an ERP refund where the detour is rider-caused. The rider's serial-claimant corroboration step under POL-RD-08 is not triggered (deviation_claims_60d = 0), and the rider's profile fields are not used against anyone.\n\nResult: NO_ACTION. Under POL-GEN-03 this is party-relative — fare_breakdown.payment_status of CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd of 0.00 stand exactly as they are; the rider is not refunded and nothing is taken back from the driver. For completeness, had the deviation survived, POL-RD-02 against the booked optimal would have given charged_total 19.69 less a recomputed_fare of 16.32 = 3.37, rounded up to SGD 3.40; that computation does not run. No clause produces a referral, and the monetary effect of zero is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold, so nothing is held and the ruling executes on issue."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

