    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver, on trip TRP-02812. The distance measurement is not in dispute. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02812) records 13.52 km against the booking's optimal distance of 10.4 km (EV-TRIP-02812) — an excess of 3.12 km, 30.0% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 thresholds and the trace is clean (100% coverage, 107 fixes, no gaps, 10-second sampling), so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07. Taken alone, that would establish a deviation and, on the arithmetic in EV-FARE-02812 (charged_total 19.69, recomputed_fare 16.32, refund 3.40), produce a refund. The deviation does not stand, because it was rider-requested. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02812) carries MSG-02812-001, sent by the rider at 10:19:39 — one minute after the meter started at 10:18:39 — asking to 'stop at Paya Lebar Square first, need to grab something'. The platform resolved the waypoint to (1.381532, 103.831811). That satisfies POL-RD-04(a), (b) and (c), and the GPS trace corroborates it: the nearest fix passes 35.99 m from the waypoint, well inside the 200 m test. Because the trace does approach the waypoint, this is not the uncorroborated-instruction case in POL-RD-14, and no POL-RD-10(7) conflict arises. The rider's argument that no artifact fixes how much of the 3.12 km the stop added is rejected. The record shows a single waypoint, hinted once; no second waypoint in the chat; no off-route ERP gantries (EV-FARE-02812 shows 0.00); and no pickup or dropoff amendment on the trip record. The one off-corridor excursion is the requested stop, so the whole measured excess is that stop's distance and POL-RD-04 excludes it. With it excluded, the excess remaining for POL-RD-01 is zero, no deviation is established, and POL-RD-02 — which runs only where a deviation is established — is never reached. The 3.40 refund in the rider's case is therefore not owed. The rider's 'quick stop, not a tour' point is fair as a description of the message, but the message asked for one specific stop and the driver made that stop; the mileage is the stop's mileage. Nothing else moves. EV-FARE-02812 carries no ERP, toll or airport surcharge line, and POL-RD-09(3) gives no ERP refund for a rider-caused detour; the driver's POL-RD-09 claim is accepted. No traffic advisory covers this window — EV-ADVIS-02812-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, and carries no fact — so no POL-RD-03 exoneration was available, though none was asserted and none is needed. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 368 completed trips in 90 days), so no POL-RD-06 conduct referral fires and no uplift applies. No driver compensation is due: billed distance of 13.5 km against the 13.52 km trace is a shortfall of 0.02 km, far under the 1.0 km gate in POL-RD-04. Ruling: NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03. On this rider-filed dispute, payment_status stays CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd stays 0.00; nothing is refunded to the rider and nothing is recovered from the driver. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor; the ruling rests on artifacts all at weight 1.0."
